  "correction_rules": [
    "Uptrend underestimation: when the last 10–15 days show a clear rising regime, add an upward bias to the whole path (model is typically ~+1 to +3 EUR too low), with the uplift increasing slightly with horizon.",
    "Horizon drift/over-extrapolation: beyond ~day 20 the model often projects an overly strong continuation move (can overshoot by +3 to +6 EUR in late-horizon), so damp late-horizon slope toward a flatter trajectory.",
    "Turning-point lag: after a local peak/trough, the model tends to react late; apply faster mean-reversion toward the recent 5–10d average when the last 3–5 days reverse direction.",
    "Spike handling: following sharp up-moves, the model either (a) fades too much early or (b) extrapolates too long late; use a two-phase rule—keep near-term closer to realized momentum (days 1–7), then cap continuation and revert toward trend (days 15–30).",
    "Volatility compression: forecast paths are too smooth versus outcomes; widen daily moves modestly (especially days 5–15) while keeping the corrected mean anchored to the adjusted trend."
  ]
}
